                    <p {...stylex.attrs(blogStyles.articleParagraph)}>
                        The PWA works fully offline through a service worker.
                        The first visit caches the ~1.8MB ONNX model, and after
                        that it works in airplane mode. I also had to write my
                        own bilinear resize in JavaScript that matches
                        PIL/Pillow's implementation exactly, so the browser
                        preprocesses images the same way the training pipeline
                        does. If the resize interpolation is off by a single
                        pixel, accuracy collapses and nothing tells you
                        why.
                    </p>

